    "chapter_title": "Mutation and the Neutral Theory"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "1. Mutation is the ultimate source of evolutionary novelty, but for most genes the rate of mutation are usually so low that mutation pressure is a weak force for changing allele frequencies.",
      "source_page": 205,
      "source_pages": [
        205
      ],
