    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "2. Despite the weak force of mutation pressure, over very long periods of evolutionary time, populations can come into equilibrium between forward and reverse mutation, when the ratio of allele frequencies equals the reciprocal of the ratio of the mutation rates.",
      "source_page": 205,
      "source_pages": [
